<http://data.silknow.org/object/1bd5c1a9-656f-3933-96c5-2324fbc3128c/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Fragment of chair cover of pink silk damask, with a border of silk brocade (in red and yellow on buff); spots of embroidery in black silk or silver thread (now oxidised) are scattered over it. Some fragments of green silk velvet were apparently part of a later covering.\n\nThe pattern on the damask consists of curved stems of peonies or lotuses. The pattern on the brocade border is a repeat based on floral motifs."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/1bd5c1a9-656f-3933-96c5-2324fbc3128c> .

